  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a large skillet over medium-high heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "While the skillet heats up, drain and rinse beans.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 (258 g) can black beans"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add beans and enchilada sauce, then stir to combine and bring to a simmer. Once simmering, reduce heat to medium and cook, stirring occasionally, until sauce is slightly thickened, about 5 minutes. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 tsp extra virgin olive oil\n1 (283 g) can red enchilada sauce"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Using a stirring spoon, make a well for each egg in the sauce; crack an egg into each well. Cover and cook until the egg whites are firm but yolks are still soft, about 5 minutes. Remove from heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, wash, dry, and shave cilantro leaves off the stems; discard stems and mince the leaves. Set aside.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ small bunch cilantro"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Warm tortillas in another skillet, oven, or microwave (optional).\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Serve the skillet \"family-style\" and allow each person to fill their tortillas with egg, sauce, and beans, adding cilantro, lettuce, crumbled cheese, and guacamole as desired. Enjoy!\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 cups shredded lettuce\n½ (283 g) block Cotija cheese\n½ cup guacamole"
    }
  ],
